{"title":"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems\">2004 AMC 12B #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems\">2004 AMC 10B #9</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square has sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and a circle centered at one of its vertices has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of the union of the regions enclosed by the square and the circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f299b8d7843afc3fc78f2ff61ab9a3d33b8a7f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ }200+25\\pi\\quad\\mathrm{(B)\\ }100+75\\pi\\quad\\mathrm{(C)\\ }75+100\\pi\\quad\\mathrm{(D)\\ }100+100\\pi\\quad\\mathrm{(E)\\ }100+125\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"641\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IGN4XxJIbE0\">https://youtu.be/IGN4XxJIbE0</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2d289bcef129fde7867462fb5618f7a8c6653d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{\\bigcirc}=100\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />; the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea14ba69c61600c2dc9dfdd8c61b1a9ab0f4f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{\\square}=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the circle lies inside the square. Thus the total area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d174c1d86c5da2a57b593979a784a4d549fb72ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac34 S_{\\bigcirc}+S_{\\square}=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)\\ }100+75\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"231\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fcea2965eceab15b23e988726a4b3446b01b59f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] Draw(Circle((0,0),10)); Draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--(0,0)); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,(5,0),S); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,(0,5),W); dot((0,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B\">2004 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title